Kind: ablation
Issue: #935
Over: 935-widen-create-terminate.patch
Takes out: the NULL check -- thread_terminate()s empty-activation branch, which the detach now routes a threadless activation to, ip_unlock()s a NULL pool port.  A deterministic fault at a small address from inside thread_terminate()
Run: --entry 14 300 -smp 4
Expect: <thread_terminate\+0x
faulting address 0x0+2[0-9a-f]

diff --git b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_act.c a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_act.c
index ee1a7746..d7131552 100644
--- b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_act.c
+++ a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_act.c
@@ -308,16 +308,8 @@ thread_terminate(
 		/*
 		 * Release locks individually. (`act_unlock_thread()'
 		 * will not work since `pool_port' field has changed.)
-		 *
-		 * 🔴 ONLY IF THERE IS ONE (#935).  act_lock_thread() locks the
-		 * pool_port when the activation has one, and a threadless
-		 * activation that never had a pool_port -- the one a failed
-		 * thread_create_in() now hands here -- has none, so this would
-		 * ip_unlock() a NULL port.  The AGRESSIVE_ABORT path above
-		 * guards it the same way.
 		 */
-		if (iplock != IP_NULL)
